# Reference index only — do NOT copy this over docker/.env. (Corrected 2026-09-06, plan task 3.3 /
# gap G12: this file used to say "copy to docker/.env", which is wrong and would break the stack.)
# `oroinc/docker-demo` ships a complete `.env` that compose reads automatically — image tags,
# ORO_DB_* credentials, the nginx/WebSocket upstream JSON. Overwriting it with this nine-line file
# strips all of that. Prime directive 7: variable names live here for reference, values live in the
# upstream-shipped docker/.env, which is gitignored and never committed.
#
# The oroinc/docker-demo stack reads these from its own .env. ORO_APP_DOMAIN is the only one this
# environment set; the rest are listed so the knobs are discoverable without reading compose.yaml.

# Domain the storefront and back-office answer on. Must match the /etc/hosts entry.
ORO_APP_DOMAIN=oro.demo

# Container-side nginx port. The host binding is fixed at 80 by the web service in compose.yaml.
# ORO_NGINX_HTTP_PORT=

# Application image and tag. Leave unset to take the upstream defaults for the current LTS.
# ORO_IMAGE=
# ORO_IMAGE_TAG=
# ORO_IMAGE_BASE_RUNTIME=
# ORO_BASELINE_VERSION=

# Postgres major version used by the db service.
# ORO_PG_VER=

# Locale variants: append the contents of .env-locale-de_DE or .env-locale-fr_FR from the clone.
# ORO_LANGUAGE_SUFFIX=
